<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Custom Login Demo</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 40px 20px;
            background: #f5f5f5;
        }

        .container {
            background: white;
            padding: 40px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }

        h1 {
            color: #333;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        p {
            color: #666;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .login-link {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding: 12px 24px;
            background: #667eea;
            color: white;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: background 0.2s;
        }

        .login-link:hover {
            background: #5a6fd6;
        }

        .protected-link {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 20px;
            margin-left: 10px;
            padding: 12px 24px;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            color: #333;
            text-decoration: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: background 0.2s;
        }

        .protected-link:hover {
            background: #e0e0e0;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Custom Login Demo</h1>
        <p>This demo shows how to create a custom login page with your own design while using the oauth2-passkey library for authentication.</p>
        <p>You are currently viewing this page as an <strong>anonymous user</strong>.</p>

        <a href="/login" class="login-link">Go to Login Page</a>
        <a href="/protected" class="protected-link">Try Protected Page</a>
    </div>
</body>

</html>
